findings.body:
**A dangling symlink into a frozen tree gets past the Rust port, where the shell hook blocks it.**

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/claude-code-config/blob/13615742b75a71b3186ede9a6fb105ee62505a32/tools/hooks-rs/src/frozen_paths.rs#L18-L22

```rust
if real.is_symlink() {
    if let Ok(target) = real.canonicalize() {
        real = target;
    }
}
```

`std::fs::canonicalize` needs every component of the path to exist, so it returns `NotFound` for a symlink whose target is missing. When that happens, `real` keeps the link's own path.

The shell hook (`.claude/hooks/frozen-paths.sh`) runs `python3 -I -c '... os.path.realpath(sys.argv[1])'`. Non-strict `realpath` follows the link to its target path even when the target is missing. This port's own comment at L6 promises the same: "resolve `..` and symlinks even through directories a Write has yet to create".

**How it is reached:** take `FROZEN_PATHS_REGEX='^packages/client/'` and a link `apps/api/alias.ts -> ../../packages/client/src/new.ts`, where `new.ts` does not exist yet. A Write to `apps/api/alias.ts` follows the link and creates the frozen file.
- Shell hook: `rel` is `packages/client/src/new.ts`, which matches, so it exits 2.
- Rust port: `rel` is `apps/api/alias.ts`, which does not match, so it exits 0. The guard fails open.

The wrong path also ends up in the allow-list line and in the deny message. Only Write can reach this, because Edit and NotebookEdit need the file to exist. The symlink fixture in `tests/frozen_paths.rs` (L43-49) only links to targets that exist, so no test covers this case.

**Fix:** on `NotFound`, `read_link` the component and resolve its target relative to the link's parent. Keep other errors, such as ELOOP, on the current fallback so a symlink loop cannot recurse forever. Add a dangling-link case to `tests/frozen_paths.rs`.

findings.suggestion:
if real.is_symlink() {
    match real.canonicalize() {
        Ok(target) => real = target,
        // A dangling link: Write creates its target, so follow it as text.
        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {
            if let Ok(target) = std::fs::read_link(&real) {
                real.pop();
                real = realpath(&real.join(target).to_string_lossy());
            }
        }
        Err(_) => {}
    }
}
